 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Not really, as long as you' acknowledging the original image. A short link like bit.ly is plenty. They' probably juiced up to think following only established artists is the only way to go. Show them you can actually sell paintings. You lose credit, and it's easy for viewer to spot. Stick with a link that says picture sourced from here, and only do it if you' reworking the background. You've got the right to use someone else's image as reference, after all. It's when people redraw it as their own work that gets sticky.",
